The DLAs that arise in this way strongly depend on
whether the graph G is bipartite (BP) or non-bipartite
(NBP), and we will consider these two cases separately.
Recall that a graph is called bipartite if its vertices can be
colored in two colors so that every edge connects vertices
of different colors.
